From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:42:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: PCI: google,gs201-pcie-cp: let the modem driver
 own the lines

The "modem" child describes the S5300's power, reset and handshake lines
so that the link driver can power the modem for bring-up without a modem
driver. Once the modem driver (Google's CPIF, ported) runs, it drives
the same lines from its own node, and a line must have one owner.

Say that the child is absent or disabled in that case, and allow its
status property.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml      | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml
index c3e58c9cf..f27f839ba 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie-cp.yaml
@@ -104,10 +104,15 @@ properties:
   modem:
     type: object
     additionalProperties: false
-    description: The modem's power, reset and handshake lines (raw levels).
+    description:
+      The modem's power, reset and handshake lines (raw levels), for
+      driving the modem without its own driver. When the modem driver
+      describes the lines in its own node instead, this node is absent or
+      disabled, so that each line has one owner.
     properties:
       compatible:
         const: samsung,s5300-modem
+      status: true
       ap2cp-pda-active-gpios:
         maxItems: 1
       ap2cp-cp-pwr-on-gpios:
